  - family-names: Banerjee
    given-names: Dipankar
abstract: >
  We introduce AutoTAB, an automated algorithm to track bipolar
  magnetic regions (BMRs) over their lifetime on the solar disk using
  MDI and HMI magnetograms (1996–2020). AutoTAB successfully tracked
  9,152 BMRs, enabling detailed study of their evolution, morphologies,
  tilt angles, magnetic fluxes, lifetimes, and statistical properties.
  The method advances understanding of solar magnetic activity cycles.
keywords:
  - Bipolar Magnetic Regions
  - solar magnetism
  - automatic tracking
  - surface flux transport
